  1. Standard Libcloud Compute API (NodeDriver)

  These are the canonical Libcloud compute methods implemented by NutanixPrismNodeDriver and used (directly or indirectly) by
  the demo.

  list_nodes(**kwargs) → List[Node]

  • REST: GET /api/vmm/{version}/ahv/config/vms
  • Demo: vm/list.py (all VMs)
  • Returns: Node objects with id, name, state, IPs, and extra (cluster, memory, NICs, disks, etc.)
  • Optional kwargs: ex_page_size, ex_page, ex_limit, ex_filter, ex_select, ex_orderby
  • Pagination: Automatic via $page / $limit (max 100)

  ex_get_node(node_id) → Node

  • REST: GET /api/vmm/{version}/ahv/config/vms/{node_id}
  • Demo: vm/list.py --id, vm/edit.py, vm/destroy.py
  • Purpose: Fetch a single VM by extId

  create_node(name, size, image, location=None, **kwargs) → Node

  • REST: POST /api/vmm/{version}/ahv/config/vms → async task in prism namespace
  • Demo: vm/provision.py
  • Required: location (cluster) or ex_cluster
  • Demo parameters:
    • --name, --image-id, --cluster-id
    • --size-id (default small)
    • --subnet-id → ex_subnet
    • --description → ex_description

